{"name":"Bonnie Blue","hex":"#8dbbd1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bonnie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Merry; happy.","Beautiful; pretty; attractive; handsome."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bonfire; chiefly one several storeys tall and burned to celebrate Eleventh Night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bonnie"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bonnie Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Tia Billinger, known professionally as Bonnie Blue, is an English pornographic film actress. After attending 2023's schoolies week, she had sex with large numbers of students at both spring break in Cancún, Mexico, and freshers' week in Derby and Nottingham, England, and went viral for discussing her sex life on GK Barry's podcast Saving Grace. She was criticised during this period for the age of her co-stars and for comments that critics have described as promoting misogyny and the sexual objectification of women."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Bonnie_Blue%2C_July_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Bonnie_Blue%2C_July_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonnie_Blue","wikidata":"Q129719542"},{"title":"Bonnie","blocks":[{"text":"Bonnie is a Scottish feminine given name. It comes from the Scots language word \"bonnie\", or the French bonne (good). That is in turn derived from the Latin word \"bonus\" (good). The name can also be used as a pet form of Bonita."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Rhett_and_Bonnie_Blue_Butler.jpg/330px-Rhett_and_Bonnie_Blue_Butler.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonnie","wikidata":"Q4689423"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Bonnie_and_Clyde_%281967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway%29.jpg/500px-Bonnie_and_Clyde_%281967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Bonnie_and_Clyde_%281967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway%29.jpg/500px-Bonnie_and_Clyde_%281967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Faye Dunaway as Bonnie Parker in the 1967 film Bonnie and Clyde.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABonnie_and_Clyde_(1967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D